@startuml
title Segmento TCP - Campos relevantes para ataques

rectangle "Cabecera TCP (20-60 bytes)" {
  rectangle "Puerto origen (16b)" as src
  rectangle "Puerto destino (16b)" as dst
  rectangle "Número de secuencia (32b)" as seq
  rectangle "Número de ACK (32b)" as ack
  rectangle "Offset (4b)" + "Reservado (6b)" + "Flags (6b)" as flags
  rectangle "Ventana (16b)" as win
  rectangle "Checksum (16b)" + "Urgente (16b)" as misc
}

rectangle flags as "Flags (6 bits)" #LightBlue {
  rectangle URG
  rectangle ACK
  rectangle PSH
  rectangle RST
  rectangle SYN
  rectangle FIN
}

note right of flags
  - SYN: inicio conexión (handshake)
  - RST: reset abrupto (ataque)
  - ACK: confirmación
  - FIN: cierre normal
  - PSH: entrega inmediata
  - URG: datos urgentes
end note

note bottom of seq
  Secuencia es crítica para:
  - Inyección RST (predecir o sniffear)
  - SYN cookies (codificar estado)
end note

@enduml